      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Despite advances in percutaneous coronary intervention, coronary artery bypass grafting remains the most effective intervention for complex coronary artery disease in survival, freedom from reintervention, and cost-effectiveness. To ensure that patients have access to this \"gold-standard\" treatment, a multidisciplinary team approach, rather than an individual cardiologist acting as a \"gatekeeper,\" should be the standard of care when intervention is necessary, to ensure transparency, real patient choice, and genuine informed consent."},
